1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,420
THIS PROGRAM INCLUDES
AI-GENERATED CONTENT

2
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:21,605
CASE 1:
THE SAINTS BASEBALL TEAM MURDER CASE

3
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:30,947
MURDER CLUB: LIAR'S TABLE

4
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:32,031
All right.

5
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:34,033
FIRST PLAYER ENTERS

6
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,452
This seems like a good spot.

7
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:38,120
Oh, boy.

8
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,081
CHOI YANGRAK
TV PERSONALITY

9
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:42,625
I guess I'm the first one here.

10
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:44,252
My goodness, what's all this?

11
00:00:44,253 --> 00:00:45,336
GRAND VIBE

12
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:46,420
[Pani Bottle] Hello.

13
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:47,505
SECOND PLAYER ENTERS

14
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:48,507
It's nice to meet you.

15
00:00:49,091 --> 00:00:50,174
I'm Pani Bottle.

16
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,509
Of course, I know who you are.

17
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,345
But I'll be playing someone else today.

18
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:55,596
PANI BOTTLE
YOUTUBER

19
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,682
I heard you have
three million subscribers.

20
00:00:57,683 --> 00:00:59,850
Not quite.

21
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,852
It's a little over two million.

22
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,271
[Max Changmin] Hello.

23
00:01:03,272 --> 00:01:04,647
- Hello, Yangrak.
- [Choi] Good to see you.

24
00:01:04,648 --> 00:01:06,065
- [Max] It's nice to see you.
- Hi.

25
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:07,441
- [Max] Hello.
- Goodness.

26
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:08,901
- [Choi] You've gotten more handsome.
- [Max] Please.

27
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,070
[Pani] It's nice to meet you.

28
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:13,365
I'm a huge fan.
I'm not just saying that for the cameras.

29
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:16,409
MAX CHANGMIN
SINGER

30
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:18,077
- It's a nice table.
- [Choi] Right?

31
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,370
They put in a lot of effort.

32
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,080
It's new leather.

33
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,958
It's not an old table.
It's been newly upholstered.

34
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:24,834
It smells new.

35
00:01:24,835 --> 00:01:27,170
You really think
they'd bring in an old one?

36
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:28,880
Hello.

37
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,090
- No way!
- Hello.

38
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:33,342
[Choi] Kim Hyunsoo.

39
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,094
- He's our MVP.
- Hello.

40
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:37,639
He's the Korean Series MVP.

41
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:40,308
[Choi] Congratulations.

42
00:01:40,309 --> 00:01:41,642
- Oh, did his team win?
- Yeah.

43
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:44,603
He won with LG
and moved to KT this season.

44
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,564
I'm sure there was a good reason.

45
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:49,317
[Pani] Was it because
they recognized his talent?

46
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:50,484
Of course.

47
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:52,069
- I don't know baseball.
- He's Korea's best.

48
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:54,947
I'm a Hanwha Eagles fan
and hoped we'd win again at last,

49
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,324
but because of this guy,

50
00:01:56,325 --> 00:01:58,284
our chances were ruined.

51
00:01:58,285 --> 00:01:59,952
Anyway, thank you.

52
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:01,829
[Kim Seontae] Hello.

53
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,497
- [Pani] I see this guy all the time.
- [Choi] Gosh.

54
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:04,582
- Hello.
- This is…

55
00:02:04,583 --> 00:02:06,083
- I saw him two weeks ago.
- Really?

56
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:07,543
- He's Chungju Man.
- Right.

57
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:08,753
Now the former Chungju Man.

58
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,171
KIM SEONTAE
FORMER PUBLIC OFFICIAL

59
00:02:10,172 --> 00:02:11,631
LOOKS AROUND

60
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:13,800
What's with your outfit?
Are you wearing sweats?

61
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:16,385
- Well, the producers called me
- Yeah?

62
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:19,555
and told me to dress formally,
but I don't have a suit.

63
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,515
You'd think a public official
would own many suits.

64
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:23,225
- Yeah.
- We're quite close,

65
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:24,894
and since we first met
about two years ago,

66
00:02:24,895 --> 00:02:27,605
he's always dressed the same.

67
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:29,774
So I once asked him
if he had any other clothes,

68
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:31,233
and he has many of the same type.

69
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:32,735
- Like a uniform?
- That's right.

70
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:34,362
Yes. I have a few.

71
00:02:34,363 --> 00:02:38,032
Did you all get briefed on today's game?

72
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:39,283
I don't know the specifics.

73
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:41,619
I was just told it was a board game.

74
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,456
They didn't give me any other details.

75
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:48,751
You're very good at board games, right?

76
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:50,795
Board games are my hobby.

77
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:53,047
- Really?
- [Pani] But I'm not good at them.

78
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:54,632
Do you play board games, Yangrak?

79
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:56,175
I play games

80
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,259
like stone-flicking.

81
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,345
UNEXPECTED ANSWER

82
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:00,429
Oh, that's right.

83
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,306
- That's a classic.
- "Stone-flicking!"

84
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,016
- We both grew up watching that show.
- Yeah.

85
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:07,229
- [Max] It was a hit program.
- [Pani] It was.

86
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,068
[host]
<i>Welcome to</i> Murder Club: Liar's Table.

87
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:15,695
- Here we go.
- Looks like it's starting.

88
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:16,779
ROUND OF APPLAUSE

89
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:19,865
<i>Today, you will be playing Murder Mystery,</i>

90
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:22,952
<i>a competitive deduction game
where your goal is to identify</i>

91
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:24,787
<i>the culprit hidden among you.</i>

92
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:27,748
<i>You will each be assigned a unique role</i>

93
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,917
<i>and play the game as that character.</i>

94
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:31,961
<i>There is only one culprit,</i>

95
00:03:31,962 --> 00:03:35,631
<i>but every player has their own secret.</i>

96
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:37,216
<i>To win this game,</i>

97
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:41,595
<i>you are allowed to lie, conceal the truth,
and act deceptively.</i>

98
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:44,682
<i>The game consists of five rounds.</i>

99
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:46,392
<i>At the start of each round,</i>

100
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:48,769
<i>one clue will be revealed
to the entire group,</i>

101
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:51,230
<i>and all the players will pick out</i>

102
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:53,649
<i>one card clue and one object clue.</i>

103
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,693
<i>The card clues are confidential</i>

104
00:03:55,694 --> 00:04:00,197
<i>and can only be shared
during private conversations.</i>

105
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:04,201
<i>The object clues
can be examined by all players.</i>

106
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:08,706
<i>After collecting the clues,
you will have a 15-minute discussion.</i>

107
00:04:08,707 --> 00:04:12,042
<i>Starting Round 2, you will have time
for private conversations.</i>

108
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:14,253
<i>After the group discussion,
you will have five minutes</i>

109
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,881
<i>to talk secretly
in the private conversation zones.</i>

110
00:04:16,882 --> 00:04:20,176
<i>In Round 5, the final round,
you will make your final vote.</i>

111
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:21,802
<i>After the final group discussion,</i>

112
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:25,474
<i>you will vote for the person
you suspect to be the culprit.</i>

113
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:27,892
I'm not sure I really get it,
but all right.

114
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:29,560
LAUGHING

115
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:31,479
Can you handle this game?

116
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,814
- There are a lot of murder mystery games.
- Okay.

117
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:35,316
They're board games

118
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:38,319
where you each play a character
and try to find the culprit.

119
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,862
I've only played it once myself.

120
00:04:39,863 --> 00:04:40,946
Was this your idea?

121
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,239
- No.
- [Choi] Did you choose this game?

122
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,909
No, I didn't know it'd be like this.

123
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,452
- He's insanely rich.
- [Pani] No, I'm not.

124
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:48,120
- So they spared no expenses.
- What?

125
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,790
How can you say that
in front of these people?

126
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,666
You're calling me rich
when I'm the poorest one here.

127
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:55,252
- He once showed his house on his channel,
- [Kim] What are you on about?

128
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:58,464
and it looked rather average,
but it was all a lie, right?

129
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:00,549
Yeah, there's a door at the very back

130
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,259
that leads to his real house.

131
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,803
- That's his real place.
- [Max] A mansion.

132
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,931
- Do you have a split personality?
- No, no.

133
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,641
Are you suspecting me already?

134
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:10,017
I think the person who'd be best

135
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:12,853
at pretending to be innocent
is Chungju Man.

136
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:14,980
- Me?
- [Pani] Yes. I know him well.

137
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:16,982
We did a survival show together,

138
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,859
and he's an expert at deceiving people.

139
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:22,071
Honestly, I didn't think
this production would be so big.

140
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:24,907
But with this kind of budget and cast,

141
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:26,325
why would they make me the culprit?

142
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:28,619
- That's a bit…
- That's true.

143
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:31,038
If I were a writer or producer,

144
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:33,624
I'd make one of you two the culprit.

145
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:36,168
But I don't have much TV experience,

146
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:39,338
and I'm new to this,
so wouldn't I be too obvious?

147
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,422
Then…

148
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:43,384
Honestly, if I might say so myself,

149
00:05:43,385 --> 00:05:47,012
I'm known for being squeaky clean.

150
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:49,348
- You're lying already.
- [laughing] No, no.

151
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:50,392
I'm not.

152
00:05:50,976 --> 00:05:53,519
- I think Pani Bottle is most likely.
- Yeah.

153
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,354
His glasses don't even have lenses.

154
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:56,730
- Yeah, they're just for show.
- See?

155
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:58,566
- See?
- It's a deceit.

156
00:05:58,567 --> 00:06:00,317
But I'm a bad liar. I share everything.

157
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:02,069
I can't lie.

158
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:03,237
Yangrak, you tell fibs.

159
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:06,282
- I'm a joke-teller.
- He's a great liar.

160
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:08,117
That's different from lying.

161
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:09,702
You lied about being sober for a year.

162
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:13,497
You told your wife for a year
that you were a teetotaler.

163
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:14,874
Oh, it was a lie?

164
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:18,127
- How can you keep up an act like that?
- It was a long time ago.

165
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,461
I'm not a good liar.

166
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:22,047
[host]
<i>Now, you will be assigned your roles.</i>

167
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:24,508
<i>Please choose one of the files
in front of you.</i>

168
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,094
CHARACTER GUIDE:
PERSONALITIES, RELATIONSHIPS, ALIBIS

169
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:31,265
THE CULPRIT HAS BEEN CHOSEN

170
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:34,685
We're now playing these characters, right?

171
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:36,186
- I'm no longer Pani Bottle.
- Right.

172
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,396
- I'm…
- You're right.

173
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,023
I'm Yoon Minseok.

174
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:40,691
<i>I'm a batting coach,</i>

175
00:06:40,692 --> 00:06:41,775
<i>and I'm 49 years old.</i>

176
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,319
<i>A batting coach?</i>

177
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,613
YOON MINSEOK
49, SAINTS TEAM BATTING COACH

178
00:06:45,614 --> 00:06:48,407
- I'm with the Saints baseball team.
- Okay.

179
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:50,367
- I'm their manager.
- [all] Ah!

180
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:52,286
<i>- You're the manager?
- Kang Dohyun, 55 years old.</i>

181
00:06:52,287 --> 00:06:53,829
<i>The manager…</i>

182
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,748
KANG DOHYUN
55, SAINTS TEAM MANAGER

183
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:59,084
I'm Jo Hajun.

184
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:00,544
- Jo Hajun.
- Yes, that's right.

185
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:03,631
<i>The main sponsor of the Saints
is Geumseong Group.</i>

186
00:07:03,632 --> 00:07:06,176
<i>- "Geumseong."
- And I'm their PR Strategy director.</i>

187
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,719
JO HAJUN
30, GEUMSEONG GROUP PR STRATEGY DIRECTOR

188
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,555
I'm Lee Hyunsoo.

189
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:12,973
- Only your surname changed.
- That's right.

190
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:14,058
I'm Lee Hyunsoo.

191
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:15,559
<i>I'm 26 years old,</i>

192
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,562
<i>and I was a rising star,
but another player surpassed me…</i>

193
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:21,940
- [all laughing]
<i>-…so now I'm just a reserve.</i>

194
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,150
What's a reserve?

195
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:26,028
- It means a backup.
- He's not in the main lineup.

196
00:07:26,029 --> 00:07:28,530
- I'm benched until someone gets injured.
- I see.

197
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,074
- Waiting for someone to get hurt.
- Yeah.

198
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:32,451
- It's the opposite of his reality.
- That's right.

199
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,495
I'm Kim Doyun,

200
00:07:34,496 --> 00:07:36,205
and I manage a fan club.

201
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,289
<i>I'm 34 years old,</i>

202
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,582
<i>and I'm a devoted fan</i>

203
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:42,253
<i>who collaborates with the team's sponsors.</i>

204
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,963
KIM DOYUN
34, PRESIDENT OF SAINTS FAN CLUB

205
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:47,049
So you don't just manage the fan club,

206
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,634
but you also have business ties, right?

207
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:49,718
Yes, that's right.

208
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,220
I play a fairly big role.

209
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:52,304
Ooh.

210
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:53,722
You can tell he's done this before.

211
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:55,392
He's already asking sharp questions.

212
00:07:55,892 --> 00:07:58,018
- [Hyunsoo chuckles]
- I've only played once.

213
00:07:58,019 --> 00:07:59,353
END OF CHARACTER INTRODUCTIONS

214
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:01,021
- It makes all the difference.
- That's true.

215
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,106
SELECTED CHARACTER RESULTS

216
00:08:02,107 --> 00:08:04,191
KIM DOYUN, KANG DOHYUN, YOON MINSEOK,
JO HAJUN, LEE HYUNSOO

217
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:09,488
[host] <i>The murder took place
in the Saints' locker room.</i>

218
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,407
<i>The victim was Park Taeo,</i>

219
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:13,576
<i>the Saints' ace.</i>

220
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:16,495
PARK TAEO
26, SAINTS' ACE BOUND FOR MAJOR LEAGUES

221
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,372
<i>Right after winning the championship,</i>

222
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:22,543
<i>he planned to expose the team's corruption
before heading to the Major Leagues,</i>

223
00:08:22,544 --> 00:08:26,463
<i>but he was discovered dead
at half past midnight that day.</i>

224
00:08:26,464 --> 00:08:29,800
<i>Here is the first shared clue.</i>

225
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:32,511
<i>Please open the envelope in front of you.</i>

226
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,847
1 SHARED CLUE IS REVEALED
AT THE START OF EACH ROUND

227
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:36,432
- Oh, gosh.
- Goodness.

228
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:38,100
OH, DEAR

229
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:39,643
ROUND 1 SHARED CLUE:
PHOTO OF THE CRIME SCENE

230
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:41,437
[Kang Dohyun] <i>There's so much blood.</i>

231
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:43,480
- <i>How badly was he beaten?</i>
- [Yoon Minseok] <i>Is that cake?</i>

232
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,733
- Cake?
- Cake and a ball.

233
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,109
It wasn't just any ordinary day.

234
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:48,694
- He just won.
- It's the day he won.

235
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:49,987
It happened right after.

236
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:52,949
- The ace was killed like this?
- How awful.

237
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:56,493
<i>Round 1 will now begin.</i>

238
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:59,456
<i>First, pick out the card clues.</i>

239
00:09:00,123 --> 00:09:05,002
<i>Every player
has a total of five card clues.</i>

240
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:09,882
<i>Each card contains a secret
that no other player knows.</i>

241
00:09:09,883 --> 00:09:13,677
<i>In every round except for the fifth round,</i>

242
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:17,139
<i>the players can take one card
from the person they suspect.</i>

243
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:21,101
<i>Use the collected clues
to determine who the culprit is.</i>

244
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:22,686
Do we pick our own cards
or someone else's?

245
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,438
Come on. Why would you pick your own?

246
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:25,857
Don't you know yourself?

247
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,443
Seeing how he just raised his voice?

248
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:31,862
- [Yoon Minseok] He seems agitated.
- I want to take one of his cards.

249
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:34,323
I guess the Saints associates
don't get along.

250
00:09:34,324 --> 00:09:35,532
I'll take the fourth card.

251
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,326
I think you could be the culprit.

252
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:38,535
[chuckling] Jeez.

253
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:40,329
KANG DOHYUN TAKES KIM DOYUN'S CARD

254
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:42,081
They each took a card from each other.

255
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:43,083
PLAYERS CAN SHARE WHAT'S ON THEIR CARD

256
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,376
OLD ENVELOPE: DOHYUN
ARRANGING ILLEGAL SPORTS BETTING

257
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,212
LAPTOP: TAEO FANDOM ANALYSIS REPORT
WRITTEN BY DOYEON, SENT TO HAJU

258
00:09:48,213 --> 00:09:49,463
I feel like

259
00:09:49,464 --> 00:09:52,258
a feud between teammates

260
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:54,177
is the most likely scenario.

261
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:57,763
There's a baseball bat in the picture,
so I suspect the batting coach.

262
00:09:57,764 --> 00:10:00,516
So I suspect the batting coach.

263
00:10:00,517 --> 00:10:01,518
Then I'll go for…

264
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:04,686
Sponsors are usually the most suspicious.

265
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,271
THE CARD CLUES HAVE BEEN SELECTED

266
00:10:06,272 --> 00:10:08,024
- Right, they're high-strung.
- [laughs] Yeah.

267
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:10,275
DOHYUN: MANAGER,
DOYUN: FAN CLUB PRESIDENT,

268
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,944
HYUNSOO: RIVAL, MINSEOK: BATTING COACH,
HAJUN: SPONSOR

269
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:14,404
Let's compare our timelines.

270
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:18,742
What were you doing and where were you
at the estimated time of the crime?

271
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:19,827
What's the time frame?

272
00:10:19,828 --> 00:10:22,412
- Between 11 p.m. and 12 a.m.
- From 11 p.m. to 12 a.m.?

273
00:10:22,413 --> 00:10:24,248
<i>My team just won,</i>

274
00:10:24,249 --> 00:10:26,834
<i>so I was doing press interviews
and appearing on the news.</i>

275
00:10:26,835 --> 00:10:31,171
<i>Likewise, I was celebrating with the team,
moving around here and there.</i>

276
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:36,844
<i>At precisely 11:50 p.m., I just went home
since everyone was busy celebrating.</i>

277
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:39,763
<i>I was celebrating
with the fan club members,</i>

278
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:42,182
<i>shaking hands
and talking to the cheerleaders.</i>

279
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:43,684
<i>I couldn't play due to an injury,</i>

280
00:10:43,685 --> 00:10:46,186
<i>so I got a checkup
from the team doctor at 11:40 p.m.,</i>

281
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:47,896
<i>and then slowly headed to the lockers.</i>

282
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,481
[Yoon Minseok]
You didn't run into Park Taeo?

283
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:50,316
- No.
- [Yoon Minseok] Hmm.

284
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:52,818
Ooh.

285
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:54,945
[host] <i>The evidence zone is open.</i>

286
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:58,782
<i>Please bring over one evidence each
and resume the group discussion.</i>

287
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,367
[Yoon Minseok]
Oh, we bring them over ourselves.

288
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:01,451
EVIDENCE ZONE

289
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:03,245
- We popped the champagne.
- Yeah.

290
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:04,913
So people were drinking.

291
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:07,834
EACH PLAYER MAY COLLECT 1 OBJECT CLUE
PER ROUND FROM THE EVIDENCE ZONE

292
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:09,835
STARTLED

293
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,254
It's the bat.

294
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,297
There's a card under it.

295
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:14,548
AN OBJECT CLUE AND A MYSTERY CARD

296
00:11:14,549 --> 00:11:16,091
I'll bring this over.

297
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,176
NOTICES SOMETHING

298
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,178
Wait.

299
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:19,846
- What?
- "Coach's bat."

300
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:22,139
- What?
- "Coach's bat."

301
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,892
ROUND 1 OBJECT CLUE:
BLOODY BASEBALL BAT

302
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:26,728
Why did they use my bat?

303
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:29,354
It's clearly a set-up.

304
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:30,856
I'm being framed.

305
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:31,983
They used my bat on purpose.

306
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,568
I'll go for locker number four.
The unlucky number.

307
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:35,987
There's blood on this ball.

308
00:11:36,738 --> 00:11:38,031
Why would a ball be used in a murder?

309
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:41,033
- [gasps] Sneakers.
- [Yoon Minseok] They're bloodstained.

310
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,784
PROMOTION PROPOSAL
GEUMSEONG GROUP PR STRATEGY TEAM

311
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:43,911
Number two.

312
00:11:43,912 --> 00:11:44,913
OBJECT FOUND

313
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,247
What's this?

314
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:48,333
It's very intriguing.

315
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,459
What is this?

316
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:51,461
WHAT'S THE FINAL CLUE?

317
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:53,880
[Jo Hajun] It seems very meaningful.

318
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,132
We're meant to share these, right?

319
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,635
We share all the object clues.

320
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:00,844
Keep your cards in your pockets.

321
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,095
CARD CLUES CAN'T BE SHOWN
DURING THE GROUP DISCUSSION

322
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,640
The first clue is already very telling.

323
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:05,642
I'll show you.

324
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:08,727
"I sometimes dream of a hurtling ball."

325
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:11,104
"Someone dies, but I survive."

326
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,189
"That's the punishment."

327
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:14,858
It shouldn't happen, but--

328
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,860
- It was written by Lee Hyunsoo.
- Yeah.

329
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:20,656
LEE HYUNSOO'S THERAPY NOTES

330
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,658
What did he mean by this?
"That's the punishment"?

331
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:24,910
Maybe it means he regrets it.

332
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:27,287
- He regrets his crime.
- Ah!

333
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:31,041
Seeing as these are therapy notes,
he must've been super stressed.

334
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:34,795
- For athletes, not being able to play…
- Right.

335
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,505
…is complete torture, right?

336
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:37,673
[Kim Doyun] That's right.

337
00:12:37,674 --> 00:12:40,384
- There's also blood on this ball.
- [Jo Hajun] Yeah.

338
00:12:40,385 --> 00:12:42,094
[Kim Doyun] Is it not related in some way?

339
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:43,887
- Look carefully at the ball.
- Yeah?

340
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:47,849
Only this part of the stitching is frayed.

341
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,101
Oh, you're right.

342
00:12:49,102 --> 00:12:51,186
[Lee Hyunsoo]
For the seam to split like this…

343
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,105
It wouldn't split like this
from hitting someone.

344
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:54,564
[Kang Dohyun]
It had to be scraped across the ground.

345
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:56,608
Or maybe it was hit by another ball.

346
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:58,694
- That'd be hard to pull off.
- Way too hard.

347
00:12:58,695 --> 00:12:59,820
- Toss batting.
- That's…

348
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,030
Maybe if you're a batting coach.

349
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:02,864
There's no way.

350
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,408
It's almost impossible.

351
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:06,952
- The bat is…
- It's labeled as "coach's bat."

352
00:13:06,953 --> 00:13:08,537
- It's the batting coach's.
- It says it here.

353
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:11,665
- Let's say I'm the culprit.
- Okay.

354
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:13,792
What kind of idiot would use his own?

355
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:15,294
There are so many bats over there.

356
00:13:15,295 --> 00:13:17,004
Look how many there are.

357
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,339
So why would I use my own to kill someone?

358
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,341
Every player has a bat
they naturally prefer.

359
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:22,634
- Isn't that right?
- That's right.

360
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,428
- They're all the same.
- Don't act naïve.

361
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:25,721
They're not all the same.

362
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:27,389
- Different weights.
- They don't weigh the same.

363
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:29,683
I thought the coach
was the most suspicious.

364
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:31,560
<i>The victim had to be killed with a bat.</i>

365
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:34,105
Accidents happen
when you're in close proximity.

366
00:13:34,856 --> 00:13:36,565
And who was closest to the victim?

367
00:13:36,566 --> 00:13:37,733
It was the coach.

368
00:13:37,734 --> 00:13:42,237
The decisive clue was the coach's bat.

369
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,865
That's what convinced me.

370
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:47,617
<i>They were probably close
until something made him snap,</i>

371
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:49,369
<i>which led to the accident.</i>

372
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:51,288
I think he's the prime suspect.

373
00:13:51,289 --> 00:13:53,165
Of course, we need to investigate
a bit more.

374
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:56,126
The bat looks clean, doesn't it?

375
00:13:56,127 --> 00:14:00,380
- Coach's bats usually are.
- That's…

376
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,965
What this proves without a doubt

377
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,633
is that I'm not the culprit.

378
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:06,636
- That came out of nowhere. Why?
- They're trying to frame me

379
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:08,221
with a weapon they didn't actually use.

380
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,890
- That's your opinion.
- Right.

381
00:14:09,891 --> 00:14:12,893
- But you're the prime suspect.
- [laughs] For now.

382
00:14:12,894 --> 00:14:14,936
It's too obvious.
The game can't end this easily.

383
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:16,980
By the way, what's this?

384
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:19,649
That's a very big bloodstain.

385
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:21,485
<i>Could he have banged
his head on the corner?</i>

386
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:22,569
DID HE HIT THE BENCH CORNER?

387
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,820
The bat wasn't swung hard enough,

388
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:26,239
so he just fainted,
but his head hit the bench,

389
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,783
and that's how he could've died.

390
00:14:27,784 --> 00:14:29,659
One swing of the bat
wasn't enough to kill him.

391
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,203
- It was a weak swing.
- He just fainted.

392
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:34,122
While falling over,
his head slammed into the bench.

393
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,626
[Lee Hyunsoo] Or maybe it was the ball.

394
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:41,713
WAS THE BALL THE REAL MURDER WEAPON?

395
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:45,050
But there's only one person here
who could throw a ball hard enough

396
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:46,134
to kill someone with it.

397
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,178
- Yeah, I agree.
- It had to be an athlete.

398
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:50,013
Are you a pitcher or a batter?

399
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,348
I'm an outfielder.

400
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:52,849
An outfielder?

401
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,685
If I had a stronger arm,
I wouldn't be a backup.

402
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:56,770
Oh, right.

403
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:58,271
You could be a one-tool player.

404
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:00,732
- All you've got is a strong arm.
- "One-tool."

405
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,025
There are players like that.

406
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:04,236
A one-tool player is unlikely
to be a backup.

407
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:08,240
You need at least two tools
to be a backup.

408
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:11,409
The ball isn't clear evidence,

409
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:14,037
<i>so I'm on the fence about Hyunsoo.</i>

410
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:15,789
<i>He doesn't have a clear motive.</i>

411
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:18,333
<i>He was jealous that Taeo was moving
to the Major Leagues,</i>

412
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,794
<i>so I don't think it was
reason enough to kill him.</i>

413
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:23,797
In my opinion, he's the only person
who has a weak motive.

414
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:27,884
I took a card from Hyunsoo earlier.

415
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:28,969
- Lee Hyunsoo's.
- Yeah.

416
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,012
I took one of his cards.

417
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:34,641
If Taeo won the game
and moved to the Major Leagues,

418
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,351
Lee Hyunsoo would benefit from it

419
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,811
- since a spot would open.
- True.

420
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:39,729
- That means he can move up.
- Right.

421
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,899
If that's the case,
why would he need to kill Taeo?

422
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:44,276
- Right, a spot would open.
- Exactly.

423
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:46,695
- There's no need.
- Yeah, it would be a good chance for me.

424
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:48,280
It's a good opportunity.

425
00:15:48,281 --> 00:15:49,531
The only motive would be

426
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:52,576
if you were on the list of corrupt people
he planned to expose.

427
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:53,785
But that's true for everyone,

428
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:56,830
including the director,
the coach, and the manager.

429
00:15:56,831 --> 00:15:59,833
- The fan club manager might be exempt.
- Yeah, I have nothing to hide.

430
00:15:59,834 --> 00:16:01,002
But the thing is…

431
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:05,172
One of the cards I picked

432
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:06,840
is about what Taeo was going to expose.

433
00:16:06,841 --> 00:16:08,425
Whose card is it?

434
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:09,801
I took it from the director.

435
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:11,052
IT BELONGED TO DIRECTOR JO

436
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:12,429
He signed it himself,

437
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:15,724
and the sponsorship and PR costs
were substantial.

438
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:17,434
- The sponsorship and PR costs?
- Yeah.

439
00:16:17,435 --> 00:16:19,436
Park Taeo's spending or his own?

440
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:20,812
It's an unofficial ledger.

441
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:23,940
<i>-No one knows what it was spent on?
- No one knows.</i>

442
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:26,776
A secret ledger for an entire team?
Is that possible?

443
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,695
It's not exactly a secret.

444
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,697
As you probably know better than anyone,

445
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:35,035
not everything the club decides
is openly disclosed,

446
00:16:35,036 --> 00:16:37,454
especially in a role like mine.

447
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:39,164
I just did what the club told me to do.

448
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:42,460
I brought up the topic
to see how he reacted,

449
00:16:43,169 --> 00:16:45,837
and it made me more suspicious.

450
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:50,300
<i>The fact that he kept
that much money off the books</i>

451
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,968
<i>suggests he was up to something.</i>

452
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:57,766
I also think he might've paid Hyunsoo
under the table.

453
00:16:57,767 --> 00:16:59,392
- I took a card from the manager.
- Okay.

454
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:01,853
This makes things a bit tricky.

455
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,480
There's an old envelope.

456
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:06,107
It's an internal document
of the Busan District Prosecutors' Office.

457
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,442
Busan District Prosecutors' Office?

458
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,611
You once broke the law.

459
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,196
What are you talking about?

460
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:13,157
You arranged illegal sports bets

461
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:14,991
and got a suspended indictment.

462
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:16,868
No, I never did that.

463
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:20,205
- You arranged illegal sports bets?
- No, that wasn't even a thing back then.

464
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:21,456
What are you talking about?

465
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,791
The time's going by so fast.

466
00:17:22,792 --> 00:17:24,417
- Yeah.
- Faster than I expected.

467
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,502
ROUND 1 CARD CLUES

468
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:28,088
OLD ENVELOPE, LAPTOP, NEWS ARTICLE,
STADIUM CLEANER'S MEMO, UNOFFICIAL LEDGER

469
00:17:28,089 --> 00:17:29,464
[host] <i>Before Round 2 begins,</i>

470
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:32,009
- <i>here is a new shared clue.</i>
- [Yoon Minseok] I'll open it.

471
00:17:32,552 --> 00:17:33,594
"October."

472
00:17:34,345 --> 00:17:37,222
"D-2, D-1. It's nearly over."

473
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:39,391
- There's a tear.
- Something's been ripped out.

474
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:41,977
"My sorrow has made another person sad."

475
00:17:41,978 --> 00:17:43,728
"It's a cycle of tragedy."

476
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,188
"I want it to end quickly."

477
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:47,607
There's nothing after that.
I think this is the last page.

478
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:50,569
- Does it belong to the culprit?
- I'm not sure what it is.

479
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,238
"I want it to end quickly"?

480
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,282
Oh.

481
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:56,825
It was mine.

482
00:17:56,826 --> 00:17:58,493
I'm not the culprit,

483
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:00,788
but I have secrets
that no one can find out.

484
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:05,250
<i>No one's focusing on that diary right now,
so that's great.</i>

485
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,835
I think we'll just slide past it.

486
00:18:06,836 --> 00:18:08,920
They'll forget all about it.

487
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,505
[host] <i>Round 2 will now begin.</i>

488
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,799
<i>Please exchange your card clues.</i>

489
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,301
The manager gets first pick.

490
00:18:14,302 --> 00:18:16,596
- You keep taking mine.
- It's because you're next to me.

491
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,763
YOON MINSEOK TAKES JO HAJUN'S CARD

492
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:20,974
- I feel compelled to take yours, Director.
- Jeez.

493
00:18:20,975 --> 00:18:22,684
I think the manager's a bit suspicious.

494
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:23,686
I think so too.

495
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,937
Why me?

496
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,814
Unbelievable.

497
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:31,026
- I also think it's you or the coach.
- We got a hard-earned victory.

498
00:18:31,027 --> 00:18:35,071
What kind of dumb manager
would kill his championship hero?

499
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,448
But you lost him to the Major Leagues.

500
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:38,450
- And you have a crime record.
- Okay.

501
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:39,827
You shouldn't accuse innocent people.

502
00:18:40,995 --> 00:18:41,996
Jeez.

503
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:43,998
Let's go.

504
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:45,833
Let's head to the Evidence Zone.

505
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:52,172
It's the locker room
security footage report.

506
00:18:52,173 --> 00:18:54,966
There's no footage
between 11 p.m. and 12 a.m.

507
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,010
It's a voice recording of Park Taeo.

508
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:58,803
Let's listen to it together.

509
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,348
This bag is full of items.

510
00:19:01,349 --> 00:19:02,433
What's this?

511
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:06,645
[Changmin inhales sharply]

512
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:08,521
A NOTE?

513
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:09,939
[Yoon Minseok] Hold up.

514
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,068
- This is a love letter.
- [Jo Hajun] Exactly.

515
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:14,444
Was it unrequited love?

516
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:18,239
We found a really unusual
piece of evidence.

517
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,991
Rather surprisingly,

518
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:23,995
there was a romance amid all this.

519
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:26,706
"Taeo, you've been pulling away."

520
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,333
"You didn't take my calls today,

521
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:29,959
and you say no one can find out."

522
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,504
It seems to be a secret relationship.

523
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,882
- Park Taeo didn't want it.
- Hmm.

524
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:38,259
I might be biased,

525
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:41,262
- but it looks like fan-letter stationery.
- Yeah.

526
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,806
It might be from a fan.

527
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:43,973
Yes, it could be from a fan.

528
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,392
- Right?
- So it might be nothing?

529
00:19:45,393 --> 00:19:46,893
[Kim Doyun] Yeah, it might be from a fan.

530
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:48,436
<i>It seemed like a fan letter to me.</i>

531
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,689
When it comes to stars and their fans,

532
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:54,859
<i>some fans can get a bit obsessed.</i>

533
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,904
<i>They express their love
in an unhealthy way.</i>

534
00:19:57,905 --> 00:20:01,991
Since it was written
on fan letter-type stationery,

535
00:20:01,992 --> 00:20:06,747
I'm suddenly very suspicious
of Kim Doyun, the fan club president.

536
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:10,125
I think this is
a fan club merchandise bag.

537
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:13,253
- Fan club merch?
- Yes, it's filled with Saints merchandise.

538
00:20:13,254 --> 00:20:14,337
A Saints key ring.

539
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:17,299
And most importantly,
there's an emergency medical kit.

540
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:21,053
It says, "Good luck, Park Taeo!"

541
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:24,514
That means he wasn't in good health.

542
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:26,182
It seems he had to take insulin shots.

543
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:27,642
- Insulin?
- Yeah, it's at the bottom.

544
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:29,561
Doesn't that mean he was diabetic?

545
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:32,856
It was well-known to his fans.
All his fans knew about it.

546
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,149
<i>He had Type 1 diabetes,</i>

547
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:37,235
<i>but he worked hard
to manage his condition.</i>

548
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:40,739
But could a fan get hold of this
on his behalf?

549
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,241
I'm not sure about that.

550
00:20:42,867 --> 00:20:45,034
What would happen
if he didn't get his insulin shot?

551
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,495
- Would he die instantly?
- He wouldn't die,

552
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:50,540
but it'd affect his performance.

553
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:52,542
If he doesn't get his shots on time--

554
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:53,626
As the team manager,

555
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:58,131
I was aware of Taeo's condition.

556
00:20:58,132 --> 00:21:00,049
- You knew about it?
- [Kang Dohyun] Of course, I did.

557
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,427
I'm his manager, after all.

558
00:21:02,887 --> 00:21:08,308
So that means these items
most likely belonged to Park Taeo.

559
00:21:08,309 --> 00:21:10,727
I thought it was a fan club bag at first,

560
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:13,646
<i>but seeing how it contains insulin
and based on what we've discussed,</i>

561
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:14,773
<i>I think it was Taeo's bag.</i>

562
00:21:14,774 --> 00:21:15,899
- I also have--
- What's that?

563
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:17,442
- I have a recording device…
- Okay.

564
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:19,820
…with a record of Taeo's calls.
I'll press play.

565
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:22,948
<i>Director Hajun.</i>

566
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:27,452
<i>I don't think I can take on
this promotion campaign.</i>

567
00:21:27,453 --> 00:21:30,122
<i>Honestly, I plan to leave the team soon.</i>

568
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:34,417
<i>So, I don't think it'd be right for me
to keep promoting the Saints.</i>

569
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:37,003
<i>I'm going to notify the club.</i>

570
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:38,214
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

571
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:41,758
END OF CALL

572
00:21:41,759 --> 00:21:43,594
What's this about, Director?

573
00:21:44,178 --> 00:21:47,430
- There was a conflict.
- You had a clash.

574
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:49,891
There were no hard feelings at all.

575
00:21:49,892 --> 00:21:54,896
<i>I worked with Park Taeo for a long time
on various promotional campaigns.</i>

576
00:21:54,897 --> 00:21:56,481
- I'm well aware of that.
- Right.

577
00:21:56,482 --> 00:22:00,026
But this season,
there were some difficulties

578
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:02,737
due to scheduling conflicts.

579
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:05,532
I think he was referring
to a scheduling issue.

580
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,283
- I don't think that was it.
- Right?

581
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:09,619
Was there a demand

582
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:11,454
for a cut of the profit?

583
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,831
A kickback?

584
00:22:12,832 --> 00:22:15,792
He and I didn't engage

585
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:19,462
in those kinds of financial dealings.

586
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:22,674
- I swear.
- I picked one of the director's cards.

587
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:27,136
He wrote an unsent text
begging him to do the campaign.

588
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:30,765
A CAMPAIGN THAT COULD
COST HIM HIS LIVELIHOOD?

589
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:34,394
It seemed like
he really wanted Taeo on board.

590
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:36,105
- He seemed desperate?
- Yes, he did.

591
00:22:36,689 --> 00:22:40,108
- He needed it to happen, so--
- That goes against what you said, no?

592
00:22:40,109 --> 00:22:43,486
Yeah, so what he just told us

593
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,864
doesn't quite align with the evidence.

594
00:22:45,865 --> 00:22:47,907
- Right. You mean his statement?
- So, that's a bit… Yeah.

595
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:53,788
As I understand it, a baseball club,
its players, and middlemen like me

596
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:56,833
<i>have multiple discussions
about whether or not</i>

597
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:58,835
<i>to move forward with a campaign.</i>

598
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:02,422
The batting coach
seemed a bit suspicious of me,

599
00:23:02,423 --> 00:23:04,424
<i>but getting suspicious
over something like that</i>

600
00:23:04,425 --> 00:23:07,385
<i>is pretty amateurish thinking.</i>

601
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:10,305
If he was planning to move next season,

602
00:23:10,306 --> 00:23:12,390
there was no reason not to do
the campaign this season.

603
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:15,226
- Right?
- I suspect something happened before that.

604
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:16,477
It was just an excuse.

605
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:19,230
Yeah, next season was just an excuse.

606
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:21,608
- It wasn't just about the campaign.
- [Lee Hyunsoo] I agree.

607
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:23,151
It wasn't just a campaign.

608
00:23:23,152 --> 00:23:25,528
It's like you said earlier.

609
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:28,323
The campaign was just an excuse.
I'm guessing there was more to it.

610
00:23:28,324 --> 00:23:30,617
In regard to that other thing,

611
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:33,494
I actually wanted to talk
about the card I picked.

612
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:34,829
- What is it?
- So the thing is,

613
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:37,916
the cards I picked
in this round and the last round

614
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:39,834
both point to the same person.

615
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:43,422
At Park Taeo's estimated time of death,

616
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:46,883
there was a witness statement

617
00:23:46,884 --> 00:23:49,510
claiming that an elderly man
entered the locker room.

618
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:50,512
CLEANING STAFF

619
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:54,557
AN ELDERLY MAN WHO ENTERED
THE LOCKER ROOM AT AROUND MIDNIGHT?

620
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,309
- An elderly man?
- What are you talking about?

621
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:57,393
Elderly?

622
00:23:57,394 --> 00:24:00,230
It says that there's no security footage

623
00:24:00,981 --> 00:24:02,148
<i>between 11 p.m. and 12 a.m.</i>

624
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:04,359
<i>-It's the only gap in the footage.
- Right.</i>

625
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,362
- Among us--
- So who made that statement?

626
00:24:06,946 --> 00:24:09,072
- Don't make things up.
- No, I'm not.

627
00:24:09,073 --> 00:24:10,740
- Are you lying for entertainment?
- No, no.

628
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:11,866
[laughing]

629
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,201
Hear me out.

630
00:24:13,202 --> 00:24:16,287
- I picked two cards, right?
- Right.

631
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:18,915
I can't go into the specifics,

632
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:23,795
but Park Taeo demanded answers
from the manager.

633
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:26,506
- Gosh.
- Do you remember what that was about?

634
00:24:26,507 --> 00:24:27,590
No, not at all.

635
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:30,426
The card I picked
also points to the manager.

636
00:24:30,427 --> 00:24:32,303
- It's about me and Park Taeo?
- Yes.

637
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:35,182
It's a note the manager wrote.

638
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:38,643
"I made that kid a champion."

639
00:24:38,644 --> 00:24:40,353
[Kang Dohyun] Yeah, I trained him.

640
00:24:40,354 --> 00:24:42,105
"But he's trying to kill me."

641
00:24:42,106 --> 00:24:43,690
- That's what he wrote.
- Park Taeo?

642
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:45,942
<i>It says, "He's trying to kill me."</i>

643
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,695
That's just a common expression.

644
00:24:48,696 --> 00:24:50,613
- Common?
- It's an everyday phrase.

645
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,532
He must've had a secret
that could be exposed.

646
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:54,367
- I have no secrets.
- Plus…

647
00:24:54,368 --> 00:24:56,119
- We found out earlier--
- You had legal trouble.

648
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:58,413
Oh, please. That was ages ago.

649
00:24:58,414 --> 00:24:59,914
- He has a criminal history.
- I don't.

650
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:01,541
Game-fixing!

651
00:25:01,542 --> 00:25:03,042
IS KANG DOHYUN A CORRUPT MANAGER?

652
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:04,627
At that time…

653
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:06,170
What are we talking about right now?

654
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,214
Who am I answering to?

655
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:10,174
- What is it you want?
- Start from the beginning.

656
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:11,467
- Say your piece.
- Whatever that is.

657
00:25:11,468 --> 00:25:14,220
- It's your last chance to defend yourself.
- When I was a teenager,

658
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:15,888
sports betting wasn't even a thing.

659
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:17,140
- And what else?
- Game-fixing.

660
00:25:17,141 --> 00:25:19,642
Why would I do something like that?

661
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:22,103
"Crime of arranging illegal sports bets."

662
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,730
<i>"Suspect, Kim Dohyun.
Suspended Indictment."</i>

663
00:25:23,731 --> 00:25:25,356
<i>You definitely have a record.</i>

664
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:27,067
A suspended indictment means

665
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:30,153
a crime was committed,
but I wasn't punished for it.

666
00:25:30,154 --> 00:25:31,404
- That's right.
- He acknowledged it.

667
00:25:31,405 --> 00:25:32,572
- He confirmed it.
- No.

668
00:25:32,573 --> 00:25:34,866
And that's got nothing to do
with this murder case.

669
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:38,703
- He pressured Park Taeo to fix the game.
- Why does it matter?

670
00:25:38,704 --> 00:25:40,955
And he thought Taeo
was going to expose him

671
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:43,416
before moving to the Major Leagues,
and that's why he…

672
00:25:43,417 --> 00:25:46,294
- You're a backup on the same team.
- Right.

673
00:25:46,295 --> 00:25:47,545
- Player Lee Hyunsoo.
- Yes?

674
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:48,714
Did I ever fix a game?

675
00:25:49,465 --> 00:25:51,257
- A backup wouldn't matter.
- He couldn't help you.

676
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:52,633
It's not like I can play.

677
00:25:52,634 --> 00:25:55,386
- No, I just mean…
- How can I fix a game?

678
00:25:55,387 --> 00:25:57,221
There aren't that many players.

679
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:59,557
Game-fixing in this era?

680
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:01,184
What a load of bull.

681
00:26:01,185 --> 00:26:02,393
Darn it.

682
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,145
This is just absurd.

683
00:26:04,146 --> 00:26:05,938
Why are you attacking an innocent man?

684
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:07,231
You lot are scary.

685
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:08,524
<i>There are too many red flags.</i>

686
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:12,737
He's the most suspicious,
based on what I know so far.

687
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:14,447
When Park Taeo exposed the team,

688
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:17,033
the person with the most to lose
was the team manager.

689
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:18,659
There were a lot of clues,

690
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:20,745
and too many of them
pointed to the manager.

691
00:26:20,746 --> 00:26:22,705
It turned out he was a criminal.

692
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:25,666
How can we play a game with a criminal?

693
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:27,461
I think they're all suspicious.

694
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:31,214
They're teaming up to get rid of me.

695
00:26:31,215 --> 00:26:34,467
There must be an accomplice.
The culprit didn't act alone.

696
00:26:34,468 --> 00:26:40,306
What kind of manager
kills his player with a bat?

697
00:26:40,307 --> 00:26:44,227
It's an unthinkable crime.

698
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:47,897
ROUND 2 CARD CLUES: ACCIDENT REPORT,
TEXT MESSAGE, HANDWRITTEN NOTE

699
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:50,441
<i>Starting Round 2,
the private conversation zones are open.</i>

700
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:55,154
[host] <i>Players can talk in private
for five minutes.</i>

701
00:26:55,155 --> 00:26:56,323
We can pick anyone, right?

702
00:26:57,074 --> 00:26:58,282
I pick Pani.

703
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,826
PLAYERS CAN PICK SOMEONE
FOR A PRIVATE TALK

704
00:26:59,827 --> 00:27:02,079
People are simple-minded.

705
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:06,083
- Come with me.
- Me? Okay.

706
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:09,168
I had some questions for the manager.

707
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:12,505
If you suspect me,
it means you're a simple-minded man.

708
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:15,174
But honestly, the bat is…

709
00:27:15,175 --> 00:27:18,386
- Come on, that's way too obvious.
- That's true.

710
00:27:18,387 --> 00:27:19,804
- But honestly,
- It's too easy.

711
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:22,890
- I called you over because you're second.
- Okay.

712
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:24,350
- I'm the second suspect?
- Yeah.

713
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:25,685
- You're second on my list.
- Okay.

714
00:27:25,686 --> 00:27:27,646
My top suspect is the manager.

715
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,648
What do you think? Who's your top suspect?

716
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:32,483
- Is motive the right word?
- Yeah?

717
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:34,944
The key issue is that Park Taeo

718
00:27:34,945 --> 00:27:36,445
- was going to blow the whistle.
- Yeah.

719
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:39,407
The people who had secrets
that could be exposed

720
00:27:39,408 --> 00:27:41,868
are the manager and director,
based on what we know so far.

721
00:27:41,869 --> 00:27:46,873
- That's right.
- That said, as for the director's motive,

722
00:27:46,874 --> 00:27:49,751
a canceled campaign
isn't reason enough to kill someone.

723
00:27:51,378 --> 00:27:52,461
There are two options.

724
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,796
That means he's not the culprit,

725
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,799
or there was more
to the promotional campaign.

726
00:27:56,675 --> 00:27:57,842
As for the manager,

727
00:27:57,843 --> 00:28:00,636
the most shameful thing
he could do in the sports industry

728
00:28:00,637 --> 00:28:02,054
that had to be kept a secret

729
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:05,099
and could even harm the industry
is game-fixing.

730
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:06,934
- It would destroy his reputation.
- Exactly.

731
00:28:06,935 --> 00:28:11,188
It could rock the entire sports industry.
That's how serious game-fixing is.

732
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:12,982
So, I suspect it's one of them.

733
00:28:12,983 --> 00:28:15,276
Are you not the culprit? Be honest.

734
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:17,153
- There's no evidence.
- Is it really not you?

735
00:28:17,154 --> 00:28:18,237
Well, there was the bat.

736
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:20,615
- You might've clashed with the players.
- Not at all.

737
00:28:20,616 --> 00:28:21,824
- Positive?
- Yeah.

738
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:23,075
Then, I change my mind.

739
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:25,202
- You're not second. You're third.
- Okay.

740
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:26,621
The second suspect is the director.

741
00:28:26,622 --> 00:28:29,291
<i>But the first suspect
is definitely the manager.</i>

742
00:28:29,875 --> 00:28:33,211
There was something
I really wanted to ask you.

743
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:35,338
Who is Cheol Ongsik?

744
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:37,465
- Who?
- Cheol Ongsik.

745
00:28:37,466 --> 00:28:39,258
I've never heard of them.

746
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:41,302
- Oh, come on.
- I mean it.

747
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:44,388
I didn't bring this up earlier
in front of the group,

748
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:47,642
but you sent money

749
00:28:47,643 --> 00:28:50,561
to someone called Cheol Ongsik.

750
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:53,940
There's a record of the transaction.

751
00:28:53,941 --> 00:28:55,524
I did no such thing.

752
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:58,486
I might've purchased
some supplies and materials.

753
00:28:58,487 --> 00:28:59,820
Supplies and materials?

754
00:28:59,821 --> 00:29:02,740
Yeah, it might be a bank transfer
for something I bought.

755
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:04,617
- But I have no idea who that is.
- All right.

756
00:29:04,618 --> 00:29:07,370
You're making it out as if

757
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:09,622
I sent money to someone
for some corrupt reason.

758
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:14,251
Hear me out. That kind of transaction
shouldn't happen.

759
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,128
- Even I know that.
- Not in this day and age.

760
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:17,213
Right, not in these times.

761
00:29:17,214 --> 00:29:18,215
But nowadays,

762
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:20,550
who wires a hundred million won?

763
00:29:21,927 --> 00:29:24,929
I've never transferred
a hundred million won. [laughs]

764
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:26,014
- Dohyun.
- Listen.

765
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:29,184
I never did that.

766
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:31,561
JO HAJUN TOOK A CARD
FROM KANG DOHYUN IN ROUND 2

767
00:29:32,145 --> 00:29:35,398
EMAIL: TRANSFER HISTORY
AMOUNT: 100,000,000 WON

768
00:29:35,399 --> 00:29:36,774
- Dohyun.
- Yeah?

769
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:39,402
- You need to be honest.
- [laughs]

770
00:29:39,403 --> 00:29:41,654
I've never been the kind of person

771
00:29:41,655 --> 00:29:45,491
to twist the facts
just to fit the narrative.

772
00:29:45,492 --> 00:29:48,327
All right, then.
Let's talk about the fan club.

773
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:51,789
<i>Did you send that letter to Park Taeo?</i>

774
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:52,873
- The fan club?
- Yeah.

775
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:54,041
- Fan letter?
- That letter we found

776
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:56,002
about how he was avoiding calls
and growing distant.

777
00:29:56,003 --> 00:29:57,045
No, I like women.

778
00:29:58,714 --> 00:30:00,548
- No, what I mean is--
- I don't like men.

779
00:30:00,549 --> 00:30:02,508
- What was your name again? Doyun.
- Yeah.

780
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:04,677
- As Doyun.
- Yeah.

781
00:30:04,678 --> 00:30:07,388
- Not as Chungju Man.
- I'm speaking as Doyun.

782
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:08,472
Does Doyun like men?

783
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,891
I might like men in real life,
but Doyun doesn't.

784
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:13,602
- Oh, it's the other way around?
- Yeah.

785
00:30:13,603 --> 00:30:15,646
Yeah, it might be
a different story in real life.

786
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:18,024
- Doyun's definitely into women?
- One hundred percent.

787
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:19,108
No doubt about it.

788
00:30:19,109 --> 00:30:22,570
Well, maybe it's not a love letter.
It could just be genuine concern,

789
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:24,447
telling him to look after himself.

790
00:30:24,448 --> 00:30:28,242
As the fan club president,
I really supported and admired him,

791
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:30,161
but interpreting it like that
is going a bit far.

792
00:30:30,162 --> 00:30:32,830
- But didn't you write it?
- No, I didn't.

793
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,124
It wasn't me. Why would I?

794
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:35,833
So you didn't write it?

795
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,502
- I brought a card with me.
- Okay.

796
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:41,673
It actually concerns the manager.

797
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,508
- He's guilty of something else.
- Ah!

798
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:49,346
But I'm holding back
until I've had a few more discussions.

799
00:30:49,347 --> 00:30:50,431
Ah.

800
00:30:50,432 --> 00:30:52,850
But he is guilty of one more thing.

801
00:30:52,851 --> 00:30:53,934
There's more corruption.

802
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:57,480
I can't go into the details,
but it's related.

803
00:30:57,481 --> 00:31:00,608
- It's related to another third party.
- Mm-hmm.

804
00:31:00,609 --> 00:31:03,652
There's a lot pointing
to the manager right now.

805
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:05,613
- I heard that he has
- Yeah?

806
00:31:05,614 --> 00:31:07,948
- another guilty secret.
- Okay.

807
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:09,825
The fan club president told me.

808
00:31:09,826 --> 00:31:11,494
- He's guilty of more corruption?
- Yeah.

809
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:13,287
This handwritten note.

810
00:31:13,288 --> 00:31:14,371
HE'S TRYING TO KILL ME

811
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:15,831
I find it the most suspicious.

812
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:18,876
He wrote about an unbeatable champion.

813
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:21,253
Park Taeo's the only one
who fits the bill right now.

814
00:31:21,254 --> 00:31:23,756
Then maybe it's this.

815
00:31:23,757 --> 00:31:26,509
Park Taeo couldn't tolerate
such corruption,

816
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:28,052
so even if it cost him,

817
00:31:28,053 --> 00:31:31,263
he felt he had to expose
the manager's misconduct.

818
00:31:31,264 --> 00:31:33,557
Who do you think is the culprit?

819
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,434
[laughing] I think it could be you.

820
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:36,519
- You suspect me?
- Yeah.

821
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:38,354
Wait. Why do you think that?

822
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:41,982
Overly devoted fans
can turn into stalkers.

823
00:31:41,983 --> 00:31:44,318
- You suspect me because I'm a fan.
- Yeah.

824
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:46,946
Park Taeo might've found you bothersome.

825
00:31:46,947 --> 00:31:48,656
He had so many fans.

826
00:31:48,657 --> 00:31:50,741
- [laughing] That's a bit…
- So if a fan is too persistent…

827
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:52,577
But the logic is a bit flawed.

828
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:55,788
I killed him because I'm such a big fan?

829
00:31:55,789 --> 00:31:58,457
- What about the insulin?
- No, maybe you were too persistent,

830
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:00,626
constantly reaching out to him,
telling him what to do.

831
00:32:00,627 --> 00:32:02,044
- Stalking?
- Yeah.

832
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:03,254
But that's--

833
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:05,882
And not to mention

834
00:32:06,591 --> 00:32:10,678
giving him insulin
and supplying him with medication.

835
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:13,055
That's a doctor's job.

836
00:32:13,056 --> 00:32:14,390
But it was sent by a fan, right?

837
00:32:14,391 --> 00:32:16,934
That's merch for the fans,
but I didn't send them.

838
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:18,352
LAUGHING

839
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:21,105
Who else among us is a fan?

840
00:32:21,106 --> 00:32:23,190
It's not like I sent it.

841
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,358
You're the fan club president.

842
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:26,026
- Yeah, I am.
- You're the most likely sender.

843
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:27,361
It's clearly from a fan.

844
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:28,655
- The fans…
- Yeah.

845
00:32:29,489 --> 00:32:30,906
That's a bit of a stretch.

846
00:32:30,907 --> 00:32:34,285
Then the bat and glove manufacturers
must be guilty too.

847
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:35,786
- Honestly, our coach
- Yeah?

848
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:38,123
- is also a bit suspicious.
- Right.

849
00:32:38,707 --> 00:32:40,291
- So I--
- He's suspicious.

850
00:32:40,292 --> 00:32:42,334
And the bat is the decisive evidence.

851
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:44,128
- You're right.
- Yeah, the bat.

852
00:32:44,129 --> 00:32:45,921
You might wonder who could be that stupid,

853
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:48,716
but that might actually be
a genius strategy.

854
00:32:48,717 --> 00:32:51,051
- To be honest--
- [host] <i>Your time is up.</i>

855
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:52,804
- <i>Round 3 will now begin.</i>
- Okay.

856
00:32:53,305 --> 00:32:54,430
Oh, man.

857
00:32:54,431 --> 00:32:56,599
I wanted to get to know the manager more.

858
00:32:56,600 --> 00:32:59,101
I wanted to see
if he acted differently in private.

859
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,896
But nothing changed.
He just kept pushing his own point.

860
00:33:01,897 --> 00:33:04,607
He suspected me, but his reasoning

861
00:33:04,608 --> 00:33:06,942
<i>was that I killed Park Taeo
because I loved him so much.</i>

862
00:33:06,943 --> 00:33:10,070
He said a fan's obsession
could lead to murder.

863
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:13,824
I just thought,
"Oh, he's talking nonsense."

864
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:16,827
I think the fan club president
is kind of twisted.

865
00:33:16,828 --> 00:33:18,997
I can't read him
even when he's right next to me.

866
00:33:19,623 --> 00:33:21,540
I can't figure out his sexuality,

867
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:24,710
<i>and the fact that he made insulin…</i>

868
00:33:24,711 --> 00:33:26,503
<i>Isn't that the job
of medical professionals?</i>

869
00:33:26,504 --> 00:33:29,340
I find that really suspicious.

870
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:32,176
<i>As for the sponsor, Director Jo</i>…
<i>Is that his name?</i>

871
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:35,763
He had some financial issues,

872
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:40,184
so I reckon he kept making
unreasonable demands.

873
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:43,938
This card shows the email record
of his transaction history.

874
00:33:43,939 --> 00:33:46,440
<i>It was deposited by Kang Dohyun,
the team manager.</i>

875
00:33:46,441 --> 00:33:49,485
<i>He sent a hundred million won
to someone named Cheol Ongsik.</i>

876
00:33:49,486 --> 00:33:52,321
What kind of crazy person
sends that much money,

877
00:33:52,322 --> 00:33:54,406
leaves a record of the transaction,

878
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:56,200
and then forgets about it?

879
00:33:56,201 --> 00:34:00,371
<i>He's the most suspicious so far.</i>

880
00:34:00,372 --> 00:34:03,249
[host]
<i>Starting Round 3, the CCTV zone is open.</i>

881
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:07,211
<i>Use the password cards
to access the security footage.</i>

882
00:34:07,212 --> 00:34:08,713
- Password?
- What password?

883
00:34:09,214 --> 00:34:12,508
- The alphabet cards we saw earlier.
- Is it this?

884
00:34:12,509 --> 00:34:13,842
<i>This was a password?</i>

885
00:34:13,843 --> 00:34:16,011
CCTV PASSWORD ON BONUS CARD
FOUND NEXT TO OBJECT CLUE

886
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:18,264
- [host] <i>Here is the third shared clue.</i>
- What's this? A cake?

887
00:34:18,265 --> 00:34:19,640
ROUND 3 SHARED CLUE: VICTORY CAKE

888
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:20,849
AND BLOOD TEST RESULTS

889
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:24,145
Oh, the baseball bat
wasn't the murder weapon.

890
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:26,313
There was a cake.

891
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:27,856
Since he was diabetic,

892
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,317
wouldn't cake be bad for him?

893
00:34:29,943 --> 00:34:31,443
WAS THE CAKE THE REAL WEAPON?

894
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:33,905
This photo's torn up.

895
00:34:35,323 --> 00:34:37,366
Check this out.

896
00:34:37,367 --> 00:34:39,911
- I think this will determine it.
- Round them all up.

897
00:34:40,495 --> 00:34:42,162
- This photo…
- What is it?

898
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:44,373
- What is it?
- Well, that solves it.

899
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:46,333
It's over. This is the decisive evidence.

900
00:34:46,334 --> 00:34:47,669
This is huge.

901
00:34:49,004 --> 00:34:51,088
Oh, there are multiple CCTVs.

902
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:52,090
Let's see.

903
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:56,427
Isn't that the director?

904
00:34:56,428 --> 00:34:57,928
[Kang Dohyun] That's him, right?

905
00:34:57,929 --> 00:34:59,471
- Yeah, it is.
- It is.

906
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:01,265
Director Hajun.

907
00:35:01,266 --> 00:35:02,391
<i>What's going on here?</i>

908
00:35:02,392 --> 00:35:04,018
<i>It looks like a family photo.</i>

909
00:35:04,019 --> 00:35:05,644
<i>Oh, my, the director…</i>

910
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:06,980
[Kim Doyun] <i>The director is the culprit.</i>

911
00:35:09,816 --> 00:35:12,444
[theme song playing]

912
00:35:42,182 --> 00:35:44,184
Translated by Hannah Og Nam
